[{"source":"MED","extId":"33499153","pmcid":"PMC7911745","annotations":[{"exact":"Contrastingly, immunodeficiency-31B is an autosomal recessive disorder affecting both the IFN-α/IFN-β and the IFN-γ pathways and therefore often causes severe and lethal mycobacterial and various other viral infections.","tags":[{"name":"IFN-γ","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000111537"},{"name":"viral infections","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0000763"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-358caebd11371f808ef46b72ad2df2dc","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"In contrast, CVID caused by heterozygous mutation in the NFKB1 gene (OMIM: 616576) has a highly variable age of onset and disease severity and is characterized by recurrent sinopulmonary infections, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and autoimmune features.","tags":[{"name":"NFKB1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000109320"},{"name":"CVID","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0015517"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-26b3b4ae99410bbd77103ad793d4d744","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"A patient with a heterozygous variant in TNFRSF1A (c.794A > G, p.K265R), which is considered a variant of uncertain clinical significance, presented with severe mucocutaneous ulcerations and pyrexia [12] after presenting with severe recurrent oral ulceration from 1 year of age.","tags":[{"name":"TNFRSF1A","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000067182"},{"name":"pyrexia","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=HP_0001945"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-b6cc2611f583d7196fe6c4e713d89fb0","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"CVID is caused by heterozygous mutation in the NFKB2 gene and is characterized by childhood-onset recurrent infections, asthma, and autoimmune features including alopecia areata and central adrenal insufficiency.","tags":[{"name":"NFKB2","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000077150"},{"name":"infections","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=OBI_1110021"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-795d836580c05d773cbece3663ebd314","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Through their actions, ADAs deactivate extracellular adenosine and terminate signaling through adenosine receptors.","tags":[{"name":"ADAs","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000196839"},{"name":"adenosine","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/compound_report_card/CHEMBL477"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-b8527f134982f31003bf74c2829529bd","type":"Gene Drug Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Through their actions, ADAs deactivate extracellular adenosine and terminate signaling through adenosine receptors.","tags":[{"name":"ADAs","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000018510"},{"name":"adenosine","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/compound_report_card/CHEMBL477"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-b62fb46074a56056cf8859da2308b5c7","type":"Gene Drug Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"ADA2 adenosine deaminase catalyzes the deamination of adenosine and 2-prime-deoxyadenosine to inosine and deoxyinosine, respectively.","tags":[{"name":"adenosine deaminase","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000196839"},{"name":"adenosine","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/compound_report_card/CHEMBL477"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-1af032843fb81c214094368fd6b053ae","type":"Gene Drug Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"In females, null or hypomorphic NEMO mutations cause incontinentia pigmenti (IP; OMIM: 308300) [32].","tags":[{"name":"NEMO","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000269335"},{"name":"incontinentia pigmenti","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0010631"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-f3f0bdf1ad45f8f1aeb29df49d645261","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"CVID is caused by heterozygous mutation in the NFKB2 gene and is characterized by childhood-onset recurrent infections, asthma, and autoimmune features including alopecia areata and central adrenal insufficiency.","tags":[{"name":"NFKB2","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000077150"},{"name":"infections","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0000544"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-80271c913d372b48b60539cf29ea1589","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Immunodeficiency-31A is an autosomal dominant disorder that selectively affects the IFN-γ pathway, but not the IFN-α/IFN-β pathway, and causes a predisposition to mycobacterial infections.","tags":[{"name":"IFN-β","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000171855"},{"name":"mycobacterial infections","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0009429"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-7f7bc85315eedca2f1a4e372f790ee28","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"MEFV (OMIM: 608107) encodes pyrin whose function as an innate immune sensor can trigger inflammasome formation, allowing the production of inflammatory mediators during infection.","tags":[{"name":"MEFV","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000103313"},{"name":"infection","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=OBI_1110021"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-10f29d236e27f6b6791f69f00723cea5","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"A 2-generation family (4 cases) carrying a heterozygous mutation in RELA (c.599+1G > A) were reported to present in their first years of life with chronic mucocutaneous ulceration and colitis (OMIM: 618287) [17].","tags":[{"name":"RELA","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000173039"},{"name":"colitis","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0003872"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-033bc42d807f2ea53832ae0ff72fbaef","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"It was reported in 1999 that TNFRSF1A mutations cause TNF receptor-associated periodic syndrome (TRAPS, OMIM: 142680) [36].","tags":[{"name":"TNFRSF1A","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000067182"},{"name":"TRAPS","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0007727"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-57da553bf3d5daca93c2847272d1157b","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Three female CGD cases where BD was initially diagnosed have been reported [12,23,24], and the genetic analysis performed on two of these cases identified mutations in NCF1. All the cases presented initially with features compatible with a BD mucocutaneous disease type, and two of them developed more typical features of CGD with severe abscesses.","tags":[{"name":"NCF1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000158517"},{"name":"CGD","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0018305"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-727c56bcc78d7974f2d9b45ee302991b","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"CVID is caused by heterozygous mutation in the NFKB2 gene and is characterized by childhood-onset recurrent infections, asthma, and autoimmune features including alopecia areata and central adrenal insufficiency.","tags":[{"name":"NFKB2","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000077150"},{"name":"CVID","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0015517"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-3b18c3c954dfa7df46abd2de8bbc3be7","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Treatments include corticosteroids, colchicine, and chlorambucil, and a TNF inhibitor with corticosteroid and colchicine was effective in one case of disease recurrence.","tags":[{"name":"TNF","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000232810"},{"name":"colchicine","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/compound_report_card/CHEMBL107"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-fd92b2dfba5d57fbc930ed7d1c9380a8","type":"Gene Drug Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Contrastingly, immunodeficiency-31B is an autosomal recessive disorder affecting both the IFN-α/IFN-β and the IFN-γ pathways and therefore often causes severe and lethal mycobacterial and various other viral infections.","tags":[{"name":"IFN-β","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000171855"},{"name":"viral infections","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0000763"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-fb65e08f8bd03e56b89d401de742ea48","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"The NADPH oxidase abnormality reduces the ability to produce active oxygen, and reduces the bactericidal ability of phagocytic cells such that the patient is susceptible to bacterial and fungal infections.","tags":[{"name":"NADPH oxidase","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000131781"},{"name":"fungal infections","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0002041"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-abe09958ee12b4196f3919ee48405582","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Periodic fevers, immunodeficiency and intermittent thrombocytopenia (PFIT, OMIM: 150550) is caused by homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in WDR1. PFIT is characterized by recurrent early-onset respiratory infections, stomatitis, cutaneous infections, and autoimmune manifestations including chronic thrombocytopenia and anemia.","tags":[{"name":"WDR1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000071127"},{"name":"respiratory infections","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0024355"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-778b5ededbb0a6a18393df477d90f79b","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"MEFV (OMIM: 608107) encodes pyrin whose function as an innate immune sensor can trigger inflammasome formation, allowing the production of inflammatory mediators during infection.","tags":[{"name":"MEFV","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000103313"},{"name":"infection","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0000544"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-c77dc120821b99871ab0f8106677f6e4","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"It has also been reported that NFKB1 mutation (c.667A < G, p.H67R) in one family (containing six cases) led to BD-like features and antibody deficiency [22].","tags":[{"name":"NFKB1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000109320"},{"name":"antibody deficiency","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0015977"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-4e364e393eca0a3cf02085b68c771b24","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Immunodeficiency-31C (OMIM: 614162) is caused by autosomal dominant gain-of-function mutations in STAT1, as reported in 2011 [38].","tags":[{"name":"STAT1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000115415"},{"name":"Immunodeficiency-31C","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0013599"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-e6195d6487325f61938aa66bef593769","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"MEFV (OMIM: 608107) encodes pyrin whose function as an innate immune sensor can trigger inflammasome formation, allowing the production of inflammatory mediators during infection.","tags":[{"name":"pyrin","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000103313"},{"name":"infection","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=OBI_1110021"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-10f29d236e27f6b6791f69f00723cea5","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"NFKB2 was first reported as the gene responsible for autosomal dominant (AD) common variable immunodeficiency (CVID) (OMIM: 615577), and this discovery was followed by NFKB1 as another gene responsible for AD-CVID [34].","tags":[{"name":"NFKB2","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000077150"},{"name":"common variable immunodeficiency","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0015517"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-3a635c4ce5d101cbff8624f58ed96939","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Additionally, NEMO deleted exon5-autoinflammatory syndrome (NEMO-NDAS), which is caused by splice-site variants, has been reported [33].","tags":[{"name":"NEMO","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000269335"},{"name":"autoinflammatory syndrome","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0019751"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-166fd0e40996e6684e73a9739724b7be","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"A case with a heterozygous mutation in LYN (c.1523A > T, p.Y508F) presented with BD-like phenotypes [12] and a history of recurrent panniculitis, abdominal pain, mouth ulcers, and testicular pain associated with fever.","tags":[{"name":"LYN","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000254087"},{"name":"panniculitis","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_1000746"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-aa12db4373c6767cb158e29a09154889","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"LIG4 syndrome (OMIM: 606593) is caused by the homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in LIG4 first reported in 1990 [37].","tags":[{"name":"LIG4","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000174405"},{"name":"LIG4 syndrome","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=Orphanet_99812"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-53c85d686bcda0190619479004e3ff47","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"MEFV (OMIM: 608107) encodes pyrin whose function as an innate immune sensor can trigger inflammasome formation, allowing the production of inflammatory mediators during infection.","tags":[{"name":"pyrin","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000103313"},{"name":"infection","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0000544"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-c77dc120821b99871ab0f8106677f6e4","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Both of the patients diagnosed with BD were successfully treated with a TNF inhibitor and the patient with neuromyelitis optica was successfully treated with an anti-CD20 antibody.","tags":[{"name":"TNF","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000232810"},{"name":"neuromyelitis optica","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0004256"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-9ea4b9121dbe17601f1ad32d93f5bb4c","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"She experienced recurrent fevers, mouth ulcers, facial and lip swelling, pustular skin lesions, myalgia and arthralgia, and had a good response to TNF-α inhibitor treatment.","tags":[{"name":"TNF-α","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000232810"},{"name":"mouth ulcers","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=HP_0000155"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-d40690bd3d7dedab48561335bef9fb45","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"A case with a heterozygous mutation in LYN (c.1523A > T, p.Y508F) presented with BD-like phenotypes [12] and a history of recurrent panniculitis, abdominal pain, mouth ulcers, and testicular pain associated with fever.","tags":[{"name":"LYN","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000254087"},{"name":"mouth ulcers","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=HP_0000155"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-16b814195f09d40746db4c30d2d944c7","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"In contrast, CVID caused by heterozygous mutation in the NFKB1 gene (OMIM: 616576) has a highly variable age of onset and disease severity and is characterized by recurrent sinopulmonary infections, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and autoimmune features.","tags":[{"name":"NFKB1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000109320"},{"name":"chronic obstructive pulmonary disease","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0000341"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-e80f7918127622b39f4efbb118729f5d","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"ADA2 adenosine deaminase catalyzes the deamination of adenosine and 2-prime-deoxyadenosine to inosine and deoxyinosine, respectively.","tags":[{"name":"adenosine deaminase","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000196839"},{"name":"inosine","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/compound_report_card/CHEMBL1556"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-4c9c6ae9ecd3760c05b54dac7ce754b1","type":"Gene Drug Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Homozygous or compound heterozygous mutations in NCF1 cause autosomal recessive chronic granulomatous disease (CGD) (OMIM: 233700).","tags":[{"name":"NCF1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000158517"},{"name":"CGD","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0018305"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-1c7cb203655cdd019ecfc8244912d88a","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"NFKB2 was first reported as the gene responsible for autosomal dominant (AD) common variable immunodeficiency (CVID) (OMIM: 615577), and this discovery was followed by NFKB1 as another gene responsible for AD-CVID [34].","tags":[{"name":"NFKB1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000109320"},{"name":"CVID","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0015517"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-aa22b92bb5e577401aeaf420ccb82e20","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Immunodeficiency-31A is an autosomal dominant disorder that selectively affects the IFN-γ pathway, but not the IFN-α/IFN-β pathway, and causes a predisposition to mycobacterial infections.","tags":[{"name":"IFN-γ","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000111537"},{"name":"mycobacterial infections","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0009429"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-f324fba7157f760a554d93b1239d1680","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"In males, the hypomorphic NEMO mutation causes X-linked anhidrotic ectodermal dysplasia with immunodeficiency (XL-EDA-ID; OMIM: 300291) [31].","tags":[{"name":"NEMO","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000269335"},{"name":"EDA","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0016535"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-40ec56da830dad721fce97bcafb17183","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"In males, the hypomorphic NEMO mutation causes X-linked anhidrotic ectodermal dysplasia with immunodeficiency (XL-EDA-ID; OMIM: 300291) [31].","tags":[{"name":"NEMO","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000269335"},{"name":"X-linked anhidrotic ectodermal dysplasia","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0010585"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-bd22e7faee4794cedcae8de0d862ef47","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"Periodic fevers, immunodeficiency and intermittent thrombocytopenia (PFIT, OMIM: 150550) is caused by homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in WDR1. PFIT is characterized by recurrent early-onset respiratory infections, stomatitis, cutaneous infections, and autoimmune manifestations including chronic thrombocytopenia and anemia.","tags":[{"name":"WDR1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000071127"},{"name":"stomatitis","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0009688"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-a2993afa9b7a6a4105dd7abb073ec202","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"CVID is caused by heterozygous mutation in the NFKB2 gene and is characterized by childhood-onset recurrent infections, asthma, and autoimmune features including alopecia areata and central adrenal insufficiency.","tags":[{"name":"NFKB2","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000077150"},{"name":"alopecia areata","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0004192"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-0904034003998178086c1ba96c2a7853","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"NFKB2 was first reported as the gene responsible for autosomal dominant (AD) common variable immunodeficiency (CVID) (OMIM: 615577), and this discovery was followed by NFKB1 as another gene responsible for AD-CVID [34].","tags":[{"name":"NFKB2","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000077150"},{"name":"CVID","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=MONDO_0015517"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-3a635c4ce5d101cbff8624f58ed96939","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"In addition, LYN-associated AID caused by a mutation in LYN was reported to be associated with early-onset autoinflammatory phenotypes such as hepatosplenomegaly, purpuric skin rashes, periorbital erythema, testicular swelling, and positive autoantibodies [47].","tags":[{"name":"LYN","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000254087"},{"name":"AID","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0000765"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7911745#opentargets-a047bb40cf1fc639a099ba4ef90f452f","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Article (http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_001029)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"prefix":"","exact":"Primary Immunodeficiency Disease","postfix":"Immunodeficiency Disease Mimic","tags":[{"name":"primary immune deficiency syndrome","uri":"http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls-concept/C0398686"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/MED/33499153#europepmc-da28ee5e4ea2a39dd29d078dea25c4f7","type":"Diseases","section":"Title (http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title)","provid